# RepoScope repository access policy

For coding tasks in this project, use RepoScope MCP as the repository context gateway.

- Start one RepoScope task session with `repo_session_start` before repository exploration.
- Use `repo_search`, `repo_read`, and `repo_context` for repository search, codebase exploration, and source reads.
- Keep the same `sessionId` for the task.
- Do not use Cursor built-in codebase search, grep, semantic search, or direct source-file reads to discover or inspect repository code while RepoScope is available.
- Do not silently bypass RepoScope if a RepoScope search/read/context call fails. Report the limitation instead.
- Acquire source incrementally. Do not request or read the whole repository by default.
- Cursor may use its normal reasoning and editing facilities after the relevant source has been obtained through RepoScope.
- Use repository-approved verification when useful.
- Finish the RepoScope task session with `repo_session_finish` when the task is complete or abandoned.

This rule controls repository context acquisition; RepoScope is not the reasoning model or editor.
